# Commit checkpoints

- Commit each coherent, completed change after the checks appropriate to it pass.
- Keep unrelated work in separate commits; avoid accumulating several completed deliverables in one large commit.
- Use clear messages that describe the resulting change, and report any verification that remains incomplete.
- Keep ride files, private databases, import manifests, and credentials out of commits.
- Push completed commits when publishing to the repository is authorized by the current task.
